==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|socle}}, from {{der|en|it|zoccolo||wooden shoe}}, from {{der|en|la|socculus}}, diminutive of {{m|la|soccus||sock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsoʊkəl/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|oʊkəl|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}
{{wikipedia}}

# {{lb|en|architecture}} A low [[plinth]] or [[pedestal]] used to display a statue or other art work.
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} The sum of the minimal [[normal]] [[submodule]]s of a given R-[[module]] of a given [[ring]] R.
# {{lb|en|mathematics|group theory}} The [[subgroup]] generated by the minimal [[normal subgroup]]s of a given [[group]].

